From: Ben Bangert <ben@groovie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] dts: rk3576-rock-4d: drive the Radxa 25W PoE+ HAT fan

The HAT switches its fan from 40-pin header pin 33 (GPIO1_C2, pwm1_6ch_2
via pwm1m1_ch2). The control is active-low: a high pin is off, which is
also the pin's reset state. Radxa's rock-4d-radxa-25w-poe overlay models
it as a pwm-fan on inverted polarity with the same five cooling levels
as the board's own fan0; the PWM driver parks an inverted channel at its
inactive (high) level when disabled, so cooling state 0 is fan off.

The thermal map entries mirror fan0's: the same two trips of
little-core-thermal as separate map entries, so each fan is an
independent cooling device of the zone. Radxa's overlay also adds a
w1-gpio node for the HAT's DS18B20 sensor; that is not ported.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
@@ -31,6 +31,14 @@
 		pwms = <&pwm2_8ch_5 0 60000 0>;
 	};
 
+	/* Radxa 25W PoE+ HAT fan on header pin 33; its control is active-low. */
+	radxa_poe_fan: radxa-poe-fan {
+		compatible = "pwm-fan";
+		#cooling-cells = <2>;
+		cooling-levels = <0 64 128 192 255>;
+		pwms = <&pwm1_6ch_2 0 40000 PWM_POLARITY_INVERTED>;
+	};
+
 	vcc_sys: vcc5v0-sys {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "vcc_sys";
@@ -348,6 +356,18 @@
 				<&fan0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
 			contribution = <8192>;
 		};
+		map5 {
+			trip = <&target>;
+			cooling-device =
+				<&radxa_poe_fan THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+			contribution = <8192>;
+		};
+		map6 {
+			trip = <&threshold>;
+			cooling-device =
+				<&radxa_poe_fan THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+			contribution = <8192>;
+		};
 	};
 };
 
@@ -597,6 +617,11 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&pwm1_6ch_2 {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pwm1m1_ch2>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &pinctrl {
 	usb {
 		usb_host_pwren: usb-host-pwren {
